.\" negative cases for generated paragraph definitions
.TH NEGATIVE 1
.SH NAME
negative \- keep prose and values
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.B -T
sets the client's key table; this is prose.
.RS 4
A prose continuation.
.RE
.PP
.B "-T sets the client's key table; this is prose."
.RS 4
Still prose, even if bold.
.RE
.PP
.B --format
.I FORMAT
.RS 4
Select a format.
.PP
.B +
.RS 4
A nested argument value.
.RE
.PP
.B -
.RS 4
Another nested value.
.RE
.RE
.PP
.B -/
.RS 4
A real symbolic flag.
.RE
.PP
.B -
.RS 4
Read standard input.
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
[\fB-N\fR \fIpartition-number\fR] \fIdevice\fR
.RS 4
Default sfdisk invocation, not a flag definition.
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fB--foo\fR \fIdoes something\fR
.RS 4
Formatted prose, not an argument placeholder.
.RE
.PP
\fB--cpu-list 0-2,6\fR
.RS 4
Numeric argument example outside OPTIONS.
.RE
.PP
\fB--split-prose\fR \fIdoes\fR \fIsomething\fR
.RS 4
Separate inline tags still form prose.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Invocations
.PP
.B --example
.RS 4
An example outside the option sections.
.RE
